    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15665" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-mōlĭor</span></b> ,
			ītus (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>inf. pass. parag.</i> emolirier, <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Bacch. 4, 5, 2</span></i>), 4, <i>v. dep. a.</i>, <i>to move out</i>, <i>bring out by
				effort</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fretum (venti),</span>”
				<i>to stir up</i>, <i>agitate</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Agam. 476</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nauseam pituitae per nares,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					8, 5, 21</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Cels. 4, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">negotium,</span>”
				<i>to effect</i>, <i>accomplish</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Bacch. 4, 5, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
